  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Ripple (asynchronous) binary counter"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A counter counts clock pulses. In an asynchronous or ripple counter only the first flip-flop receives the external clock; each following flip-flop is clocked by the output of the previous one. With JK flip-flops (J = K = 1) or T flip-flops (T = 1) each stage toggles and divides the frequency by 2. With n flip-flops the counter has $2^n$ states, 0 to $2^n - 1$, and is called MOD-$2^n$. For negative-edge-triggered flip-flops, clocking each stage from Q of the previous one gives an up counter; clocking from $\\bar{Q}$ gives a down counter."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "n flip-flops → MOD 2ⁿ, counts 0 to 2ⁿ − 1"
    },
    {
     "en": "Each stage divides the frequency by 2"
    },
    {
     "en": "Q to next clock: up; Q̄ to next clock: down (negative edge)"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "In a ripple counter the clock drives only the first flip-flop, and each output clocks the next. n flip-flops count from zero to two to the n minus one.",
    "kn": "ರಿಪಲ್ ಕೌಂಟರ್‌ನಲ್ಲಿ ಕ್ಲಾಕ್ ಮೊದಲ ಫ್ಲಿಪ್-ಫ್ಲಾಪ್ ಅನ್ನು ಮಾತ್ರ ಚಾಲನೆ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ; ಪ್ರತಿಯೊಂದರ ಔಟ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಮುಂದಿನದಕ್ಕೆ ಕ್ಲಾಕ್. n ಫ್ಲಿಪ್-ಫ್ಲಾಪ್‌ಗಳು 0 ಯಿಂದ 2ⁿ − 1 ರವರೆಗೆ ಎಣಿಸುತ್ತವೆ."
   },
   "formula": "\\text{MOD} = 2^n, \\qquad f_{n} = \\frac{f_{clk}}{2^n}"
  },
