  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "MOD-N and decade counters"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "For a MOD-N counter choose the smallest n with $2^n \\ge N$, and clear all flip-flops the moment the count reaches N, using a NAND gate on the outputs that are 1 in N. A decade (MOD-10, BCD) counter uses 4 flip-flops and clears at 1010, so the NAND inputs are $Q_3$ and $Q_1$; it counts 0000 to 1001. IC 7490 is a decade counter. Because each flip-flop waits for the one before it, delays add up: with propagation delay $t_{pd}$ per stage the clock period must exceed $n\\,t_{pd}$."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Flip-flops needed: smallest n with 2ⁿ ≥ N"
    },
    {
     "en": "Decade counter: clear at 1010 via NAND(Q3, Q1); IC 7490"
    },
    {
     "en": "Ripple delay: f_max ≈ 1/(n·t_pd)"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A decade counter uses four flip-flops and a NAND gate that clears them when the count reaches ten, one zero one zero. Ripple counters are slow because the delays add up.",
    "kn": "ದಶಕ ಕೌಂಟರ್ ನಾಲ್ಕು ಫ್ಲಿಪ್-ಫ್ಲಾಪ್‌ಗಳು ಮತ್ತು ಎಣಿಕೆ 1010 ತಲುಪಿದಾಗ ಅವನ್ನು ಶೂನ್ಯಗೊಳಿಸುವ NAND ಗೇಟ್ ಬಳಸುತ್ತದೆ. ವಿಳಂಬಗಳು ಕೂಡುವುದರಿಂದ ರಿಪಲ್ ಕೌಂಟರ್ ನಿಧಾನ."
   },
   "formula": "f_{max} \\approx \\frac{1}{n\\,t_{pd}}"
  },
